{
  "$comment": [
    "Judgement-only champion traits, keyed by Riot's champion id (the Data Dragon key).",
    "",
    "Everything that can be read from a real source is NOT in here: damage type comes from OP.GG,",
    "and class tags, attack range and defensive rating come from Data Dragon. This file holds only",
    "the things no API reports, and only for champions whose behaviour is well established.",
    "",
    "A champion that is absent is treated as neutral: the rules that depend on these fields simply",
    "do not fire for it. That is deliberate. Guessing a value for a champion nobody here has seen",
    "would dress invention up as measurement, and the composition advice would be worse for it.",
    "",
    "  engage    0 none · 1 conditional or short-range · 2 reliable, team-wide initiation",
    "  peel      0 none · 1 some · 2 strong protection for a carry",
    "  cc        0 none · 1 slows and nudges only · 2 reliable single-target hard CC",
    "            3 long or multi-target hard CC",
    "  scaling   early · mid · late",
    "  waveclear 0 poor · 1 adequate · 2 strong",
    "",
    "Since 2.1, only where the profile is clear (absent = neutral, the plan rules skip it):",
    "  poke      1 some damage from range before a fight · 2 the core of the kit",
    "  split     1 can hold a side lane alone · 2 built to split-push: wins 1v1, takes towers",
    "  pick      1 can catch a single target · 2 a reliable catch from range or out of sight",
    "",
    "Edit freely; the file is read at start-up and anything unparseable falls back to neutral."
  ],
